<h2>Course notes</h2>
<p>Every module in the outline above links to its full lecture notes. Each follows one chapter of Bishop's
  <em>Pattern Recognition and Machine Learning</em>, the course text, and explains the same ideas in its own words: the
  model and its assumptions, the derivations that matter, NumPy code written from scratch with its real output, checks
  of that code against closed forms or brute force, figures, and exercises. The notes and the chapter support each
  other; the book has the complete derivations and many more exercises.</p>
